From a6c030cfd9dd847da4821edafd4dc379631bb047 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:55:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report the Oplus gauge voltage
 and current in uV/uA

The Oplus charger firmware's fuel gauge snapshot gives the battery voltage in mV and the current in mA, but
power_supply expects uV and uA (as the USB supply and the gauge's own capacity values already are). The Pad 4
reported VOLTAGE_NOW=3871 while its PMIC log says VBAT 3873 mV. Scale both by 1000.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 6d717ef8fb..ec2b607895 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1784,8 +1784,9 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_oplus_gauge_callback(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 
 	battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
 	battmgr->status.temperature = le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_TEMP]);
-	battmgr->status.current_now = -(s32)le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_CURRENT]);
-	battmgr->status.voltage_now = le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_VOLTAGE]);
+	/* the gauge reports mA and mV; power_supply wants uA and uV */
+	battmgr->status.current_now = -(s32)le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_CURRENT]) * 1000;
+	battmgr->status.voltage_now = le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_VOLTAGE]) * 1000;
 	battmgr->status.percent = le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_SOC]) / 100;
 	battmgr->status.capacity = le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_REMAINING]) * 1000;
 	battmgr->status.soh_percent = le32_to_cpu(data[OPLUS_GAUGE_SOH]);
-- 
